  },
  data: {
    LLM: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
    Player: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
    objective: 'Capture cards from the layout. First player/team to reach target score (usually 11 or 21 points) wins.',
    gameplay: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
    keyRules: [
      '2-4 players, 4 in partnerships, anticlockwise',
