      equipment: 'Standard deck, score sheet',
      dealing: "Player to dealer's right cuts 4 cards from middle of deck to form initial layout. Dealer deals all cards to players one at a time. First dealer random; deal passes right. If initial layout has 3+ points in scoring cards or 3+ picture cards, reshuffle and recut.",
    },
    turnFlow: "Captured cards kept face up in single pile. New captures on top. Capturing card must be on top. You can sort captured cards but opponents don't see the order. Partners share a pile in 4-player game. Layout: 4 initial cards, can be captured or added to. Builds: Single build (sum=value) or Augmented build (multiple sets with same value). Build owner must capture it eventually. Turn: Must play exactly one card from hand. Actions (in any order, before/after playing): 1) Capture (chow) - play card to capture matching card(s) or builds, 2) Create single build, 3) Change build value, 4) Create/add to augmented build, 5) Discard to layout. Can only do one of actions 1/3/5 per turn (involve playing card). Can do multiple of actions 2/4 without playing card. Cannot capture directly from opponent's pile, but can use top card in augmented builds. Drifting: Playing a card that could capture but using it in build instead - legal but opponents can insist on capture if you try to leave capturable cards. Capturing card must go on top of pile.",
